From 10f9f7bfab3509702d220bf7bd9291912c1ed231 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fozzfut <vanolia13@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:04:41 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Gui: every absolute camera placement and every seek stops the
 running camera motion (issue 038)

Round 3 of the class "absolute camera placement while a camera motion runs".

- View3DInventorViewer overrides resetToHomePosition (Std_ViewRestoreCamera,
  "RecallWorkingView" = End key): the Quarter restore copies the saved camera
  absolutely and left a FixedTimeAnimation running, which then turned the
  restored pose about its old rotation centre. It now stops the running motion
  first when there is a saved camera.
- A Coin seek (timed absolute flight to a point) is a camera motion too:
  SoQTQuarterAdaptor::endSeek(finish) ends it (stop where it is, or at its end
  pose). A navigation animation started while a seek runs ends the seek first
  (NavigationStyle::startAnimating, like NavigationAnimator::start stops a
  running animation), so the seek's end no longer stops the new turn;
  View3DInventorViewer::seekToPoint stops a running view animation before the
  seek starts; setCameraOrientation/translateCamera end a seek next to their
  stock animator stop; the fits finish a running seek like a running animation;
  View3DInventorViewer::stopAnimating (Python view.stopAnimating) stops both.
- Uniform order check, stop, place in setViewDirection and
  viewDefaultOrientation (orientation lock checked before anything stops).
- setSeekMode keeps its stock effect (navigation animation only).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
